 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nBigQuery column qualification broken after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nColumn qualification for BigQuery queries is not working properly. When using the `qualify_columns` optimizer with `dialect=\"bigquery\"`, columns are not being properly qualified with table names.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot import optimize\n\nsql = \"\"\"\nSELECT a, b \nFROM table1 t1 \nJOIN table2 t2 ON t1.id = t2.id\n\"\"\"\n\n# This should qualify columns with table aliases\nresult = optimize(sql, dialect=\"bigquery\", rules=[\"qualify_columns\"])\nprint(result)\n```\n\nExpected output should have columns qualified like `t1.a, t1.b` but they remain unqualified as `a, b`.\n\nThe issue seems to affect BigQuery specifically - other dialects work as expected.\n</issue>\n",
